  "definition": "Dexamphetamine, also called dextroamphetamine, is the d-form of amphetamine. It is a central nervous system stimulant and sympathomimetic that has been used for narcolepsy and attention deficit and hyperactivity problems, and it also has abuse potential and can produce psychosis-like effects.",
